{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1000", "sample_idx": 26, "model_name": "meta/llama-3.3-70b-instruct", "content": "Raymond III Count of Tripoli was a Count of Tripoli from 1152 to 1187 he was the son of Raymond II Count of Tripoli and Hodierna of Jerusalem. He played a significant role in the history of the Crusader states during the 12th century. \n*Early Life* \nRaymond III was born around 1140 to Raymond II Count of Tripoli and Hodierna of Jerusalem his mother was the daughter of King Baldwin II of Jerusalem and the sister of Queen Melisende and Count Alphonso-Jordan of Toulouse. \n*Reign* \nRaymond III became the Count of Tripoli in 1152 after the death of his father he was still a minor at that time and the regency was held by King Baldwin III of Jerusalem. \n*Captivity and Release* \nIn 1164 Raymond III was captured by Nur ad-Din Zangi the emir of Aleppo during the Battle of Harim he was imprisoned for several years before being released in 1173. After his release Raymond III married Hodierna's niece also named Hodierna. \nRaymond III was a skilled military leader and he played a significant role in the Battle of Montgisard in 1177 where the Crusader forces led by King Baldwin IV of Jerusalem defeated the forces of Saladin. \n*Later Life and Death* \nRaymond III died on September 1187 without an heir his death led to a succession crisis in the County of Tripoli. He was succeeded by Bohemond IV of Antioch who was the grandson of Bohemond II of Antioch and Alice of Jerusalem. \nRaymond III was also known for his conflicts with the Kingdom of Jerusalem and the Principality of Antioch he was a strong advocate for the independence of the County of Tripoli and he resisted the attempts of the Kingdom of Jerusalem to exert control over the county. \n*Legacy* \nRaymond III is remembered as one of the most important figures in the history of the County of Tripoli he played a significant role in the politics and military conflicts of the Crusader states during the 12th century. His legacy continued to shape the history of the region for centuries after his death. \nRaymond III was a complex figure who played a significant role in the history of the Crusader states his life and reign were marked by conflicts and power struggles but he also achieved significant military victories and maintained the independence of the County of Tripoli.", "logprobs": [{"token": "Ray", "logprob": -9.775113539944869e-06}, {"token": "mond", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " III", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " Count", "logprob": -0.0009117737063206732}, {"token": " of", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " Trip", "logprob": -3.576278118089249e-07}, {"token": "oli", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " was", "logprob": -0.00015948931104503572}, {"token": " a", "logprob": -0.5847842693328857}, {"token": " Count", "logprob": -0.4840473532676697}, {"token": " of", "logprob": -4.887569048150908e-06}, {"token": " Trip", "logprob": -9.417489309271332e-06}, {"token": "oli", "logprob": -1.0728830375228426e-06}, {"token": " from", "logprob": -0.05688214302062988}, {"token": " ", "logprob": -3.933898824470816e-06}, {"token": "115", "logprob": -2.3841855067985307e-07}, {"token": "2", "logprob": -8.344646857949556e-07}, {"token": " to", "logprob": -0.006717361975461245}, {"token": " ", "logprob": -6.9141146923357155e-06}, {"token": "118", "logprob": -1.311301275563892e-06}, {"token": "7", "logprob": -1.1920928244535389e-07}, {"token": " he", "logprob": -0.15241791307926178}, {"token": " was", "logprob": -0.01152948196977377}, {"token": " the", "logprob": -0.08933473378419876}, {"token": " son", "logprob": -0.03225897625088692}, {"token": " of", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " Raymond", "logprob": -7.271740287251305e-06}, {"token": " II", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " Count", "logprob": -0.0016480210470035672}, {"token": " of", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " Trip", "logprob": -3.576278118089249e-07}, {"token": "oli", "logprob": -8.344646857949556e-07}, {"token": " and", "logprob": -1.19209282